---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import StatusLists from "../components/StatusLists.astro";
import PineTexture from "../components/PineTexture.astro";
import FactTable from "../components/FactTable.astro";

const tree = "https://github.com/OGShawnLee/pino-lang/tree/main";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Status"
  description="0.4 ships the new compiler as pino; the older compiler is retired."
>
  <Hero>
    <Fragment slot="title">Status and roadmap</Fragment>
    <p slot="lead">
      Pino is a one-person project. 0.4 ships the new compiler as <code>pino</code>; the older compiler is retired.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <section class="status" id="pine" aria-labelledby="pine-title">
    <PineTexture place="section" />
    <div class="wrap inner">
      <p class="label">Status</p>
      <h2 id="pine-title">Growing slowly,<br /><span class="poem">as a pine tree does.</span></h2>
      <StatusLists
        worksLabel="Strengths"
        notYetLabel="Weaknesses"
        works={[
          "Small, readable syntax, with one obvious way to do most things.",
          "Data can't change behind your back, which makes code easy to reason about and review.",
          "No <code>null</code>; failures are values the checker makes you handle.",
          "Error messages written for people.",
          "Planned performance close to C: native code through C compilers, no GC, no pauses, low memory use.",
          "A complete written spec with a conformance test for every rule.",
        ]}
        notYet={[
          "Young, and a one-person project.",
          "Small standard library and no package ecosystem yet.",
          "No concurrency yet.",
          "Structures that point at each other need <code>Pool</code> and handles instead of pointers, which takes some getting used to.",
          "AI models know very little Pino yet.",
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section label="Parts" id="parts">
    <Fragment slot="title">Where each part stands</Fragment>
    <FactTable
      caption="Where each part of Pino stands"
      head={["Part", "State"]}
      rows={[
        [
          "VM",
          "The default for <code>pino run</code>, the REPL and the browser playground. Runs the whole language.",
        ],
        [
          "C backend",
          "<code>pino build</code>, <code>pino run --c</code>: C99 with its own reference-counting runtime. TinyCC is bundled on Windows only; Linux and macOS use the system C compiler. <code>--release</code> uses GCC or Clang.",
        ],
        [
          "Tests",
          "<code>pino test</code>, with <code>test</code> blocks and asserts that show values.",
        ],
        [
          "Conformance",
          "Every rule in the spec has tests; both engines pass all 657 cases with the same output.",
        ],
        [
          `Self-hosted compiler (<a href="${tree}/projects/pino-compiler/"><code>projects/pino-compiler</code></a>)`,
          "In progress, written by hand in Pino.",
        ],
        [
          "Editor support",
          `Syntax highlighting for <a href="${tree}/vscode-pino/">VS Code</a> and <a href="${tree}/zed-pino/">Zed</a>.`,
        ],
      ]}
    />
  </Section>

  <Section label="Next" id="roadmap">
    <Fragment slot="title">Roadmap</Fragment>
    <ol>
      <li>Faster native string building (next).</li>
      <li>A faster VM: startup under 0.1 s, closer to Python's speed.</li>
      <li>The reference-counting optimizations (Perceus-style reuse) and arenas, for 0.5.</li>
      <li>Concurrency, calling C libraries, and a "Pino for LLMs" page.</li>
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Decisions" id="decisions">
    <Fragment slot="title">Recently decided</Fragment>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Structs and collections are values, copied on write, with <code>mut</code> parameters to change the caller's
        value.
      </li>
      <li><code>Option[T]</code> replaces <code>null</code>.</li>
      <li>Type annotations go after the name: <code>val n int = 12</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      The details are in <a href={`${tree}/spec/decisions/`}><code>spec/decisions/</code></a>.
    </p>
    <p class="more"><a href="/performance/">How fast it is</a></p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .text {
    max-width: 40rem;
    color: var(--soft);
  }
  .note {
    max-width: 36rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--soft);
  }
  .more a {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
    padding-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }
  .more a::after {
    content: " →";
  }
  .more a:hover {
    color: var(--pine);
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .status {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .status .inner {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: 1.25rem 3rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .status h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.4rem;
  }

  ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 1.4rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  ol li {
    padding: 0.2rem 0;
  }
  ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  ul li {
    padding: 0.2rem 0 0.2rem 1.4rem;
    text-indent: -1.4rem;
  }
  ul li::before {
    content: "— ";
    color: var(--pine);
  }
</style>
